<!--
  Corta's Sparkle update feed. Read by every launched Corta at the interval
  the `SUScheduledCheckInterval` key in `Sparkle-Info.plist` sets, and on
  demand from Check for Updates… (`Corta/UpdateController.swift`).

  Hosted from this path, unmodified, via raw.githubusercontent.com — see
  the `SUFeedURL` key in `Sparkle-Info.plist`, the target's INFOPLIST_FILE.
  No separate server: pushing an updated copy of this file to `main` *is*
  publishing an update.

  <item> entries are appended by `scripts/release.sh` against the archive
  `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds, signs and notarizes — never
  written by hand. Each one carries an `sparkle:edSignature` over the exact
  archive it describes, produced by Sparkle's own `generate_appcast` against
  the private half of `Sparkle-Info.plist`'s `SUPublicEDKey`. A hand-typed
  entry is a hand-typed signature, which defeats the point of having one.
-->
